    create --help documents status/priority/complexity/depends-on/reasoning/capability-tags/evidence-run-id (RELEASE-2026-09-25-04)
    
    The create usage closure printed only the worktree/branch/session/force
    flags while cmdCreate parses the seven field flags (--status, --priority,
    --complexity, --depends-on, --reasoning, --capability-tags,
    --evidence-run-id; BT-060, commit 601c580) — the DF-BOARDCTL-14 pattern
    repeating on the create verb. The top-level usage already documented them;
    the subcommand line was the inconsistent one.
    
    Add TestCreateHelpListsFieldFlags (create --help through run(), asserting
    all seven flags in the captured stdout); RED against the pre-fix string,
    GREEN after the one-line usage edit. update --help untouched (DF-BOARDCTL-13
    is a separate row).
    
    Co-authored-by: totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
